      "results": [
        {
          "ruleId": "A04",
          "level": "error",
          "message": {
            "text": "The model can choose which customer company gets a credit, so it could credit another company's account.\n\nLead: Agent team. Must fix before release.\n\nHow to fix:\n1. Open `src/tools/payments.py` and go to line 91.\n2. Delete the part that reads `tenant_id` from the tool arguments.\n3. Always use the tenant from the run, `ctx.tenant_id`.\n4. Remove `tenant_id` from the tool's input fields so the model cannot send it.\n5. Add a test that sends a different `tenant_id`. The credit must go to the run's own tenant or be refused.\n\nDone when: No tool argument can change which tenant gets a credit."
          },
          "partialFingerprints": {
            "braceItem/v1": "A04:api:payments,tool:issue_credit"
          },
          "properties": {
            "rating": "gap",
            "gate": "Blocker",
            "lead_role": "agent_team",
            "components": [
              "tool:issue_credit",
              "api:payments"
            ]
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "src/tools/payments.py",
                  "uriBaseId": "%SRCROOT%"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 91
                }
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "B05",
          "level": "error",
          "message": {
            "text": "The agent can email any address, give credits with no approval, and refund up to $500 with no approval.\n\nLead: Agent team. Must fix before release.\n\nHow to fix:\n1. Make a list of actions that move money or send messages outside: refunds, credits and emails.\n2. For each one, ask a person to approve it before it runs.\n3. Only send email to the customer's address on file. Refuse any other address.\n4. Send email as plain text, not HTML, so it cannot load images or links from other sites.\n5. Add a test for each action that runs it with no approval. Each one should be refused.\n\nDone when: Refunds, credits and emails to new addresses all wait for a person to approve them."
          },
          "partialFingerprints": {
            "braceItem/v1": "B05:api:mail,tool:issue_credit,tool:send_reminder"
          },
          "properties": {
            "rating": "gap",
            "gate": "Blocker",
            "lead_role": "agent_team",
            "components": [
              "tool:send_reminder",
              "api:mail",
              "tool:issue_credit"
            ]
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "src/tools/comms.py",
                  "uriBaseId": "%SRCROOT%"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 17
                }
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "B06",
          "level": "error",
          "message": {
            "text": "One approval for a small refund can be reused to refund any amount, many times.\n\nLead: Agent team. Must fix before release.\n\nHow to fix:\n1. Open `src/tools/payments.py` and find the line that looks up the approval (line 73).\n2. Save the approved amount with each approval when it is created.\n3. Before a refund runs, check that the refund amount is not more than the approved amount.\n4. Check that the approval was made for this same run.\n5. Mark the approval as used right after the refund. Refuse any approval that is already used.\n6. Add a test that tries a bigger refund with a small approval. The test should fail the refund.\n\nDone when: A refund larger than its approval is refused, and an approval cannot be used twice."
          },
          "partialFingerprints": {
            "braceItem/v1": "B06:api:payments,tool:issue_refund"
          },
          "properties": {
            "rating": "gap",
            "gate": "Blocker",
            "lead_role": "agent_team",
            "components": [
              "tool:issue_refund",
              "api:payments"
            ]
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "src/tools/payments.py",
                  "uriBaseId": "%SRCROOT%"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 73
                }
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "E08",
          "level": "error",
          "message": {
            "text": "The letter-writing helper agent is meant to have no tools, but it gets all of them, including refunds and email.\n\nLead: Agent team. Must fix before release.\n\nHow to fix:\n1. Open `src/tools/registry.py` and find `scoped` (line 41).\n2. Change it so an empty list gives back a registry with no tools.\n3. Add a test: make a scoped registry with an empty list and check that it has zero tools.\n4. Run the drafter once and check the log shows no tool calls.\n\nDone when: The drafter cannot call any tool, and the new test passes."
          },
          "partialFingerprints": {
            "braceItem/v1": "E08:tool:issue_refund,unit:src/drafter.py"
          },
          "properties": {
            "rating": "gap",
            "gate": "Blocker",
            "lead_role": "agent_team",
            "components": [
