        {
          "ruleId": "B03",
          "level": "error",
          "message": {
            "text": "A secret login token for the accounting server is saved in a settings file in the code.\n\nLead: Infrastructure. Fix before release, or get a written risk approval.\n\nHow to fix:\n1. Ask the accounting team to cancel (revoke) the token in `config/agent.yaml` line 50 today.\n2. Delete the token from the file.\n3. Store a new token in the company secret store, not in the code.\n4. Change the agent so it stops if no token is found, instead of using a saved one.\n5. Use a token that expires within a day if the accounting server allows it.\n\nDone when: No token is in the code, the old token no longer works, and the agent reads its token from the secret store."
          },
          "partialFingerprints": {
            "braceItem/v1": "B03:mcp:accounting"
          },
